  "id": "tolerance",
  "term": "tolerance",
  "definition": "Tolerance is a decreased response to a drug after repeated use, so larger amounts are needed to get the same effect that a smaller amount once produced. This can happen because the body changes how it processes the drug or because the person adapts at cellular, physiological, or behavioral levels.",
